	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S. P.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Agitur nunc annus, theologorum decus <persName ref="p495">Bulingere</persName>, <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>quod nihil literarum ad te dedi.<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1"><persName ref="p8073">Cousins</persName> letzter Brief war vom 25. März 1546 (<bibl source="b19">HBBW XVI</bibl>, <ref target="file12440">Nr. 2393</ref>).</note></s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Quid istud? inquis; <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>anne mei de te tam bene meriti oblivisceris?<pb type="edition" next="375"/></s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Ego <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>vero, si te unquam observavi vel colui (ut nihil feci <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>religiosius)<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Dieses und alle weiteren Klammerpaare ergänzt.</hi></note>, tui etiamnum observantissimus sum et <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>intimis heres precordiis!</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div2" corresp="regest2">
				<p>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Litteras autem quod ad te <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>tam raro do, plura in causa sunt.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Primum negotia <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>tua cęlestia, quibus cum toti orbi prosis,<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Angesprochen wird hier <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Tätigkeit als Ausleger der Schrift; vgl. z.B. <bibl source="b19">HBBW XVI</bibl> 262.</note> ne ego importunior <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>haec conturbem (ad que quam maxime adhortatum <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>oportuit), in scribendo sum subsegnior.<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">weniger eifrig; s. <bibl source="b316">Hoven</bibl> 538.</note></s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Deinde si quid <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>otii ab huiusmodi negociis superest (ut parum superesse <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>satis scio), hoc innumeris literis a doctissimis quibusque<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> quibuque.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>undelibet terrarum<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">undelibet terrarum: von wo auch immer.</note> ad te missis impartitur.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Postremo <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>mihi vix unquam datur aliquid ocii et raro contingunt <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>recta euntes <placeName ref="l28">Basileam</placeName>, quibus tuto committam literas, <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>et si maxime contingant, is est nunc temporum status, ut non <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>expediat omnia literis credere.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Vides etiam hanc meę taciturn<lb xml:id="p1z18"/>itatis rationem constare, quod, ne tua studia interpellentur, <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>precipua omnibus cura esse debet.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div3" corresp="regest3">
				<p>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">In <placeName ref="l822">Germania</placeName> novis <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>tragoediis plena sunt omnia.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Interea nos cochlearum in <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>morem contracti latitamus<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Vgl. <bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl> 4, 4, 57 (<bibl>ASD</bibl> II/7 213f, Nr. 3357).</note> in horas extrema expectantes.</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z22"/>Iampridem certe vidimus nihil superesse nisi, ut dominum <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>rogemus, ut nobis prestet, quod <persName ref="p21112">Pallas</persName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6"><persName ref="p21112">Pallas Athene</persName>, griechische Stadtgöttin von <placeName ref="l1887">Athen</placeName>.</note> olim <placeName ref="l1887">Atheniensibus</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>credita est pręstitisse, videlicet ut hominum inconsulta consilia <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>vertat in bonum exitum.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Mundus omnibus suis copiis et <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>opibus insurgit in Christum,<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Ps 2, 2</ref></cit>.</note> et<ptr target="fnd" type="footnote" n="d"/> quo meliores ac religiosiores sunt <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>nostri pirgopolinices<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">= pyrgopolinices: Prahlhanse; s. <bibl source="b353">Kirsch</bibl> 2349.</note>, hoc facilius illis imponitur ab his, qui <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>lupos ovillo vellere dissimulant.<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Mt 7, 15.</ref></cit> - Gemeint sind die schlechten Bischöfe.</note></s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Sed Christus vivit!<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Lk 24, 5</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Röm 14, 11</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Apk 1, 18</ref></cit>.</note></s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div4" corresp="regest4">
				<p>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Utinam <lb xml:id="p1z29"/>mereamur, ut nobis expergiscatur<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">Zu verstehen ist: dass es uns klar wird.</note> (vel cecis apparet<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Vgl. <bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl> 1, 8, 93 (<bibl>ASD</bibl> II/2 315f, <ref target="file10832">Nr. 793</ref>).</note>), quid in <lb xml:id="p1z30"/><placeName ref="l1107">Tridentino</placeName> actum sit consilio<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Diese Orthographie verbirgt eine Pointe; s. <ref target="file13009">Nr. 2960</ref>, <ptr target="qvfn17225-4" type="qv"/>. - Zum Konzil s. zuletzt <ref target="file13020">Nr. 2971</ref>, <ptr target="qvfn17237-1" type="qv"/>.</note>, ut in ecclesia maneant mala <lb xml:id="p1z31"/>simul cum bonis.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Mala suapte natura crescent, bona decrescent,<pb type="scan" next="v."/> <pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>ut solent.<note xml:id="fnd" type="footnote" n="d"><hi>Der hier folgende Wortlaut findet sich auch in einem Brief von <persName ref="p8073">Cousin</persName> an <persName ref="p164">Bonifacius Amerbach</persName> vom 7. Juli 1547 (<bibl>AK</bibl> VI 500, <ref target="file13019">Nr. 2970</ref>).</hi></note></s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Utcumque sit, etiam si fractus illabatur orbis,<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14"><hi><persName ref="p19882">Horaz</persName>,</hi> Carmina, 3, 3, 7.</note> id<note xml:id="fne" type="footnote" n="e"><hi>Fehlt in der Vorlage.</hi></note> non me distrahet <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>a consortio ecclesiae Christi.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">De premio viderit dominus ipse.<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Mt 16, 27</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>Röm 2, 6</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>1Kor 3, 8,</ref></cit> etc.</note></s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div5" corresp="regest5">
				<p>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p1278">Gastius</persName> <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>noster, proximis tuis litteris edoctus opinor,<note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16">Sollte dies der Fall gewesen sein, ist dieser Brief <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> an <persName ref="p1278">Gast</persName> nicht mehr erhalten.</note> firmioris tue valetudinis <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>nos nuper commonuit, quo nuncio mirum in modum delectatus sum.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z5"/>Faciat dominus, ut ecclesiae Christi quam diutissime supersis!<pb type="edition" next="376"/></s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div6" corresp="regest6">
				<p>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Dominum <lb xml:id="p2z6"/><persName ref="p8171">Theodorum Bibliandrum</persName>, virum praeter singularem eruditionem <lb xml:id="p2z7"/>etiam optimum, meo nomine plurimum salutabis.</s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p1283">Guesnero</persName> video <lb xml:id="p2z8"/>quantum debeam, et meminero.<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Vermutlich hatte <persName ref="p1283">Konrad Gessner</persName> <persName ref="p8073">Cousin</persName> ein Exemplar seiner <hi>Bibliotheca universalis</hi> als Geschenk zukommen lassen; vgl. nämlich <bibl source="b19">HBBW XVI</bibl> 263,21-23.</note></s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">Tu mihi nunc apud illum fueris epistolę <lb xml:id="p2z9"/>vice rogans, ut pergat sui similis esse.</s>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la" ana="salute"><persName ref="p8127">Conrado <span type="pronoun">item</span> Pellicano</persName>, viro <lb xml:id="p2z10"/>Hebraicę linguae ac rei theologicę impense perito, et <persName ref="p8412">Gaspari Megandro</persName><note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18"><persName ref="p8412">Kaspar Megander</persName> war bereits am 17. August 1545 gestorben; s. <bibl source="b18">HBBW XV</bibl> 481.</note>, <lb xml:id="p2z11"/>theologo vere summo, tum <persName ref="p8459">Otthoni Werdmillero</persName> trium linguarum<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19">Gemeint sind Hebräisch, Griechisch und Lateinisch.</note> <lb xml:id="p2z12"/>ac omnium artium peritissimo, <persName ref="p4554">Rodolpho Collino</persName> Gręco et <persName ref="p167">Ioanni <lb xml:id="p2z13"/>Iacobo Amianno</persName><note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20"><persName ref="p167">Johann Jakob Ammann</persName>.</note> plurimam ex me salutem dices, sed precipue singulari <lb xml:id="p2z14"/>amico meo <persName ref="p8011">Rodolpho Gvaltero</persName>, nam vereor, ne nunc non vacet omnibus <lb xml:id="p2z15"/>scribere.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
			<div xml:id="div7" corresp="regest7">
				<p>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la">Cura valetudinem tuam, domine et preceptor incomparabilis, <lb xml:id="p2z16"/>et fortem animum fac obtineas teque, ut soles, in his fortune procellis tua <lb xml:id="p2z17"/>virtute sustineas.</s>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la">Quod vero ad <persName ref="p1278">Gastium</persName> aut <persName ref="p18340">Sigismundum Gelenium</persName><note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21"><persName ref="p18340">Sigismund Gelenius</persName>, Editor und Korrektor bei <persName ref="p8353">Froben</persName> in <placeName ref="l28">Basel</placeName>.</note> <lb xml:id="p2z18"/>miseris, tuto ad me perveniet.<ptr target="fnf" type="footnote" n="f"/></s>
					<s n="27" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l356">Nozerethi</placeName>, calendis augusti 1547.</s>
					<s n="28" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z19"/>Agnosce manum subscribentis, quęso<note xml:id="fnf" type="footnote" n="f"><hi>Mit einer anderen (feineren) Feder und von <persName ref="p8073">Cousins</persName> eigener Hand geschrieben.</hi></note>.<note xml:id="fn22" type="footnote" n="22">Offensichtlich wagte es <persName ref="p8073">Cousin</persName> nicht, mit seinem Namen zu unterschreiben; vgl. nämlich das in oben Z. <ptr target="qvzl17240-1" type="qv"/>. <ptr target="qvzl17240-2" type="qv"/> Gesagte.</note></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Ohne Adresse.]</note>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
